codex
The focused Rust regression passes, and its anti-vacuity checks are sound at the core level. However, the Python-facing object currently has no `content_beta_estep` field and explicitly constructs the recompute stub with `None`, so I’m validating that this causes the claimed exact-recompute behavior to fail through the public API.
