     8	
     9	### Fixed
    10	
    11	- **STM content-model ν recompute (#442):** for a content (covariate-word) STM,
    12	  `_recompute_eta_cov` rebuilt every document's variational covariance ν against
    13	  the group-averaged β instead of the document's own group β, so the recomputed ν
    14	  (used for method-of-composition uncertainty when `keep_eta_cov=False`) did not
    15	  match the fit's. It now rebuilds ν against each document's group β. A fresh fit
    16	  carries a new `content_beta_estep` snapshot (the group β active during the final
    17	  E-step, the content analogue of `beta_estep`) and reproduces the stored ν
    18	  exactly; a loaded model uses the persisted per-group `content_beta` (off by the
    19	  final content M-step, still far closer than the group average). Non-content
    20	  models are unchanged. Save-format note: the per-document group index is now
    21	  persisted, so an STM **content** model saved by an earlier version cannot be
    22	  loaded by this one (the trailing bincode field fails at EOF; `#[serde(default)]`
    23	  does not migrate positional saves — see #443). Refit to recompute exactly.
    24	
    25	- **SAGE correctness (#422):** the opt-in `convergence_tol` early stop tripped at
    26	  iter 20 (before any content-deviation `κ` was learned), because with `κ=0` the
    27	  monitored word log-likelihood is a corpus constant; it is now gated on a completed
    28	  `κ` update. Added input validation (`alpha > 0`, `lbfgs_iters >= 1`,
    29	  `num_samples >= 1`, finite non-negative `convergence_tol`, no duplicate
    30	  `group_names`), a guard that skips (and warns on) a non-finite `κ` optimization
